Desired Competencies and Attributes
In-depth understanding of the Competency-Based Curriculum (CBC) structure, objectives, and outcomes.
Ability to implement learner-centered approaches and integrate core CBC competencies (e.g., creativity, communication, and critical thinking).
Competence in using ICT tools and digital platforms to enhance learning and assessment.
Familiarity with educational technologies that support CBC teaching.
Commitment to ongoing learning and professional growth to stay updated with CBC developments.
Team player with the ability to work with colleagues, parents, and the wider school community.
Commitment to ethical practices, confidentiality, and responsibility in handling learners and curriculum delivery.
A genuine interest in fostering growth and learning among junior secondary students.
Ability to take initiative in class, co-curricular activities, and school projects.
Precision in preparing learner portfolios, lesson plans, and assessments
