The overall purpose of the job is to oversee the daily operations and management of the preschool while ensuring the school is providing a safe, nurturing, and educational environment for the children that is in line with best practices and the institution’s policies and procedures.
Duties and Responsibilities
Oversee the daily operations of the pre-school, ensuring that it is running smoothly and efficiently;
Develop and implement policies and procedures for the pre-school in liaison with the Deputy Head of School;
Develop and implement curricula and lesson plans that align with the set Ministry of Education curriculum guidelines and school requirements and policies;
Monitor and evaluate the effectiveness of the pre-school's educational programs and make necessary recommendations for improvements and adoption;
Manage and maintain accurate records of student enrolment, attendance, and progress;
Evaluate student progress and implement interventions as needed to ensure that all students are meeting academic and social-emotional milestones;
Accurately prepare pre-school meeting and events reports and submit to the Deputy Head of School;
Conduct regular staff meetings and professional development sessions to ensure that all staff members are aligned with the school’s mission and values in liaison with the Deputy Head of School;
Ensure compliance with all relevant laws, regulations, and standards related to early childhood education;
Respond to inquiries from parents and other stakeholders in a timely and professional manner;
Foster a positive and inclusive school culture that values diversity and promotes respect and kindness among students and staff;
Collaborate with parents and other stakeholders to ensure that the school is meeting the needs of the children and their families;
Ensure the preschool environment is clean, safe, and well-maintained;
Assist the Deputy Head of School in Planning and budgeting for educational trips and events within the school;
Prepare and submit the Pre-school’s requisitions list to the Deputy Head of School for approval e.g. books and stationeries;
Attend meetings and conferences to stay up-to-date on the latest research and best practices in early childhood education; and
Any other responsibilities assigned to the job holder by the supervisor from time to time
Qualifications
Bachelor in Early Childhood Education from a recognized institution
Must be registered with the Teacher Service Commission (TSC)
Minimum of 4 years relevant experience in Education
Desired Competencies and Attributes
Proficiency in using Microsoft Office
Strong knowledge of early childhood education theories and best practices.
Proficiency in using educational technology tools and platforms
Should be an effective communicator with the ability to handle both internal and external correspondences
Should demonstrate a proven track record in educational leadership such as classroom administration and instructions, lesson plans and pupil assessment
Ability to design lessons that teach curriculum in an engaging manner, applying various teaching methods
Strong supervisory and leadership skills to manage and control the department and assigned classroom
Should demonstrate ability to think and act critically and creatively
Should demonstrate ability to identify and respond to risk areas within the department
Should have effective people management and conflict resolution skills
Should be keen to detail
Understanding of child development and behavior
Ability to work collaboratively with staff, students and parents
go to method of application »

Job Summary
The overall purpose of the job is to oversee all academic and examination processes in line with the school’s curriculum and supervise all Academic Heads of Departments.
Duties and Responsibilities
Plan, monitor the teaching and learning process in order to achieve the set learning and teaching objectives;
Supervision and allocation of duties amongst the teaching staff ensuring there is balance and alignment to the role mandate;
Preparation of timetables – exams, lessons and remedial classes/sessions to ensure that all the subjects are covered and there is even distribution of subjects and avoid clashing of classes;
Coordination of the examination process, by ensuring the exams are set, reproduced and implementation of the same and ensure that the marks have been uploaded in the system within the set timelines ;
Ensure that the uploaded grades have gone through the verification process to ensure all the marks are captured accurately before releasing to the learners;
Monitor lessons delivery and collect attendance data for the teachers doing remedial classes for overtime analysis;
Target setting for the teaching staff and reward system as a way of motivation for both the faculty staff and the learners to maintain high performance;
Organize benchmarking trips to other schools to pick lessons, trends and compare with KISC for improvement;
Student management to ensure their welfare both academics, emotional and physical wellbeing is adhered;
Responsible for knowledge transfer (teaching) to the learners by using the prescribed teaching methods and in accordance with the set syllabus;
Create assessment timelines and scheduling CAT’s and examinations; ensuring formal assessments and marking schemes are of high quality;
Monitor general student enrolment to help determine if certain subjects should be eliminated or new ones introduced to tap full student potentials;
Evaluate effectiveness of the school programs in preparing students for exams and transition to higher learning;
Where necessary, communicate with parents any relevant information on academic needs, challenges and progress of the students;
Track and monitor class attendance registers every week and alert the Head of School on anomalies in student records and/or teacher absenteeism;
Guide students on making selections for courses of study – college/university, advise on the evolving job market that influence career choices;
Coordinate the requisition of teaching and learning materials in good time; and
Any other responsibilities assigned to the jobholder by the supervisor from time to time.
Qualifications
Bachelor’s degree in Education from a recognized institution.
Must be registered with Teacher Service Commission (TSC)
Minimum of 4 years’ relevant experience in British Curriculum.
Desired Competencies and Attributes
The ability to design lessons that teach curriculum in an engaging manner, applying various teaching methods such as lectures, discussions, demonstrations, and individual or collaborative projects and research.
Strong supervisory and leadership skills to manage and control the classroom.
Excellent verbal and written communication skills.
Excellent interpersonal skills with the proven ability to maintain professionalism and tact in high-stress situations.
Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail.
Creative analytical and problem-solving skills.
ICT skills
Knowledgeable in the area of specialization
Good communication skills (both verbal and written) as well as presentation skills
Ability to counsel students
Responsive to the needs of a dynamic student population
Ability to build positive relationships with students, parents and employees
Team player
Ability to solve problems
go to method of application »

Job Summary
The overall purpose of this job is to provide students with a safe and inclusive learning environment by designing and implementing appropriate learning instructions and activities that align with the curriculum and manage overall student discipline.
Duties and Responsibilities
Responsible for the preparation of schemes of work and lesson plans for the section;
Ensure smooth/seamless change-over from one activity/lesson to the next during class time;
Develop and carry our assessment of the learners based on the content – both summative and formative in line with the term syllabus;
Set exams, ensure they have been reviewed by the section lead, administer the same, mark and upload results into the system;
Responsible for safeguarding the well-being of the learners both physically and emotionally;
Escalate matters that are contrary to the expected learner behavior to the relevant office;
Counsel and guide the learners as and when needed and escalate when higher interventions are required;
Provide spiritual guidance to the learners according to the various faiths; ensure the learners attend their various religious classes as per the timetable;
Conduct remedial classes for those learners that have learning gaps or lagging behind in some areas;
Help to identify learners who have special needs and recommend interventions for specialized support;
Teach life skills to the learners on issues to do with relationships, environmental preservation, global citizenship;
Organize, and coordinate class activities, sports days and excursions for the class and attend the same;
Develop activity and school budgets for approval by the Head of School at the beginning of the term;
Participate in rotational school duties as and when required;
Ensure the mission and vision of the school are communicated and explained clearly to the learners;
Collaborate with the quality assurance department and implement feedback/recommendations provided afterward;
Prepare teaching aides and presentations, learning materials for the learners in a timely manner;
Prepare monthly reports on performance, class activities, trips and any updates relevant to the class; and
Any other responsibilities assigned to the jobholder by the supervisor from time to time
Qualifications
Bachelor of Education, Major in Art and design or related field
Must be registered with the Teacher Service Commission (TSC)
Minimum of 3 years of teaching experience
Desired Competencies and Attributes
Must have ability to plan, organize, implement and evaluate departmental goals
Must demonstrate ability to handle multiple and conflicting priorities, and work under strict deadlines.
Must have strong written and verbal communication skills to work with students, parents, fellow teachers and administrators
Must demonstrate ability to create and teach effective lesson plans related to the subject
Must demonstrate subject matter expertise to teach the topics effectively
Must have knowledge of behavior management strategies to keep students engaged and learning
Must demonstrate Strong organizational and time management skills
Must be Creative and with engaging presentation skills
Must be confident in using technology to enhance student learning
Must be resourceful and be able to teach effectively given the available resources and student skill levels
Must be results-oriented with the ability to deliver the desired outcome
go to method of application »

