Job Summary
The overall purpose of this job is to provide students with a safe and inclusive learning environment by designing and implementing appropriate learning instructions and activities that align with the curriculum and manage overall student discipline.
Duties and Responsibilities
Ensure safe transportation of pupils to and from school by conducting pick-up and dropoff duties, while maintaining appropriate safety procedures when in transit;
Develop daily lesson plans that incorporate the CBC framework and deliver lessons on numeracy, literacy, and understanding of the world to students;
Create a nurturing, stimulating, and safe learning environment for early year’s pupils and assess their progress and adaptability;
Coordinate and facilitate the school trips and excursions, including selecting appropriate destinations, ensuring adequate transportation and ensuring the safety and well-being of all pupils. The role should also evaluate the effectiveness of the trips/excursions and make improvements for future trips;
Develop a termly scheme of work outlining the topics, expected outcomes, and resources to be used for each lesson;
Prepare a daily occurrence report on classroom happenings and maintain accurate records of the students’ work;
Organize and lead school assemblies twice a week on Mondays and Fridays, including coordinating pupil presentations and selecting those that would lead the assembly;
Administer enrolment interview assessments for potential pupils, analyse the results, and key in the grades into Mzizi system whilst providing feedback to parents on their child's results and responding to questions they may have;
Develop a term-based theme and related projects focusing on life skills, culture, and other related areas;
Conduct end-of-unit assessments to evaluate student understanding of the material covered and analyze the results to determine the effectiveness of the teaching methods used;
Maintain a safe and healthy learning environment by ensuring that the classroom is safe, clean, and well-organized;
Supervise students during classroom and outdoor activities to prevent accidents and promote positive behaviour;
Participate in ongoing professional development such as seminars and workshops to stay up-to-date with best practices in early childhood education and teaching methodologies to enhance teaching skills and knowledge;
Create a safe and stimulating learning environment by setting up displays, and bulletin boards that engage children's curiosity and support their learning;
Communicate regularly with parents and guardians about their child's progress, strengths, and areas of improvement through regular parent teacher conferences, progress reports, and other forms of communication;
Assist in setting up beds for nap time after lunch and closely supervise pupils during nap time to ensure their safety and well-being;
Provide differentiated instruction to meet the diverse needs of early year’s students.
This includes using a variety of instructional strategies, materials, and resources to support student learning and success;
Foster a positive classroom culture that promotes respect, inclusion, and empathy by establishing clear expectations for behaviour and providing students with opportunities to collaborate and work together;
Provide assistance with toileting and potty training, including changing diapers as needed;
Any other responsibilities assigned to the jobholder by the supervisor from time to time.
Qualifications
Diploma in Early Childhood Education or a related field.
Must be registered with Teacher Service Commission (TSC)
Minimum of 2 years relevant experience in Education
Desired Competencies and Attributes
Experience with play-based learning and student-centered instruction.
Experience in classroom management and creating a safe and inclusive learning environment.
Knowledge of Early Childhood Education. Understanding of developmentally appropriate practices, educational theories, and strategies specific to early years.
Ability to design and deliver age-appropriate lessons, activities, and assessments that align with the curriculum and learning objectives.
Ability to use formative and summative assessments to evaluate student learning and adjust instruction accordingly.
Ability to create and maintain a safe, organized, and engaging learning environment.
Ability to integrate technology into instruction and use technology to support student learning.
Ability to speak different languages and communicate with parents who may speak different languages.
Understanding of phonics and early reading instruction to help students develop their reading skills.
Ability to use and integrate various classroom technologies and educational software to enhance learning patience and empathy.
Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues, parents, and other stakeholders to support student learning and well-being.

Responsibilities
Within delegated authority, the Human Rights Officer (Investigator) will be responsible for the following duties: Researches, collects and analyses information and documentation pertaining to human rights and international criminal law matters as required by the mandate, and, under the guidance of the Investigation Team Leader, proposes investigative methods and tools;
Conducts investigations, including through interviews with victims and witnesses, to gather information and corroborate allegations of violations of international human rights or criminal law as stipulated in the Fact-Finding Mission’s mandate;
Conducts timely monitoring of trends and patterns of violations;
Employs monitoring and mapping tools and multi-source, including open sources material and satellite imagery, to support geolocation of incidents and to assess the authenticity of collected materials and testimonies; - Identifies alleged perpetrators based on agreed information gathering methods;
Participates in and organizes missions to sites of violations or other places as required;
Ensures that all measures are taken for the protection of victims and witnesses who will cooperate with the Fact-Finding Mission according to the agreed methodology and respect for the 'do no harm principle', and by making effective use of pathways for survivors;
Ensures that the information and documentation related to the investigation is protected, stored and preserved safely in accordance with procedures established by the Fact-Finding Mission;
Undertakes preliminary analysis of information gathered and drafts analytical documents, including a gender analysis;
Drafts relevant sections and provides inputs for the Fact-Finding Mission 's report;
Ensures that gender perspective and gender-sensitive approaches are integrated at all stages of the investigation, analysis and report drafting;
Performs other related duties as required.
Education
Advanced university degree (Master's degree or equivalent degree) in law, political science, international relations, social sciences or related field.
A first-level university degree in combination with two additional years of qualifying work experience may be accepted in lieu of the advanced university degree.
Work Experience
A minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible work experience in human rights is required.
A minimum of two (2) years of experience carrying out investigations of violations of international human rights law, international humanitarian law or international criminal law is required.
Relevant working experience in or on the region is desirable.

The Enforcement Officers will be responsible for maintaining order within the County, safeguarding property, ensuring public safety in collaboration with various stakeholders in the County. The Enforcement Officers will report to the Head of Security in the County.
Requirements for appointment
Enforcing County Acts and regulations e.g on Revenue collection, physical planning, environment etc;
Assist in implementation of an immediate response to security incidents utilizing appropriate surveillance equipment; response to emergencies as and when need arise;
Ensure public order and sanity in markets, bus parks and other business areas within the County, including traffic control;
Make security recommendations to senior officers and share intelligence information;
Guarding and securing County Governmnent buildings, resources and vital installations;
Any other relevant duties as may be assigned from time to time.
Assisting the customer care desk staff in receiving and directing visitors to relevant offices;
Ensure proper records are kept for necessary action;
For appointment to this grade, an officer must have;
Providing security to select officers in the Executive in key functions and as required;
Must be a Kenyan citizen;
Kenya certificate of Secondary Education (KCSE) Mean Grade of D(plain) or its equivalent from the Kenya National Examination Council or equivalent examination bodies;
Basic knowledge of relevant legislation;
Compliance with Chapter Six of the Constitution of Kenya, 2010;
Skills on Musical Band and NYS training will be an added advantage.

Key Responsibilities:
Draft, review, and negotiate contracts, agreements, MOUs and other legal documents with external partners;
Ensure all contracts comply with legal and organizational standards;
Manage the contract lifecycle, from initiation to renewal or termination.
Monitor and ensure compliance with local, national, and international laws and regulations;
Develop and implement compliance policies and procedures;
Conduct regular compliance audits and risk assessments.
Provide legal advice and support for the management of external grants;
Ensure all grant agreements meet compliance requirements and organizational goals;
Assist in the integration of all functions into the grants management process.
Contribute to the development and updating of organizational policies related to contracts and compliance;
Provide training and support to staff on legal and compliance issues.
Work closely with Finance, HR, Procurement, Communications, and ICT teams to ensure cohesive support for the DSPPGM office;
Act as a liaison between DSPPGM and external legal counsel when necessary.
Liaise with legal departments in the Ministry of Health, Attorney General's office, National Treasury, Ministry of Foreign Affairs, and other relevant governmental bodies in management of contracts;
Ensure alignment with governmental policies and regulations affecting contracts and compliance.
Provide legal advice on intellectual property , including patents, trademarks, copyrights, and trade secrets;
Assist in the protection and management of intellectual property assets;
Develop and implement policies related to IP
Vacancy Requirements:
At least four (4) years relevant work experience; Mandatory
Bachelor of Laws degree from a recognized institution; Mandatory
Four (4) years post admission as an advocate of the High Court Kenya; Mandatory
Postgraduate Diploma in Legal Studies from the Council of Legal Education; Mandatory
Membership to the Law Society of Kenya (LSK); Mandatory
Supervisory course lasting not less two (2) weeks from a recognized institution; Mandatory
Valid practicing license; Mandatory
Proficiency in computer applications; Mandatory
Demonstrated work performance and results. Mandatory
Attention to detail Mandatory
Problem-Solving and Critical thinking Mandatory
Strong Communication Skills Mandatory
Leadership and Management Mandatory

RU/AFP/01/12/24
Job Description
An officer at this level shall:
Provide health education to clients regularly on identified health needs to help prevent diseases;
Measure and record patients’ vital information such as temperature, weight and blood pressure to help maintain good health;
Examine, diagnose and treat diseases and injuries to restore health to patients;
Complete health records of patients to capture health conditions and healthcare services offered to help in data collection; ~
Administer medication to patients and counsel them to help restore their health;
Maintain records of drugs used after working hours to avoid wastage and stock-out;
Evaluate patients’ health outcomes by scheduling them for review visits when necessary to help restore their health;
Conduct minor surgical procedures such incision and drainage of abscesses to help restore health;
Decontaminate, clean, dry and sterilize used medical instruments and equipment to prevent spread of diseases;
Order and interpret medical tests as need arises so as to ascertain/confirm diagnosis before treatment;
Refer routine and emergency patients for investigation or specialist attention to avoid complications; and
Perform any other duty as may be assigned from time to time.
Job Specification for Appointment
For appointment to this grade candidates must have:-
Successfully completed three (3) year pre-service training in a recognized institution.
Diploma in Clinical Medicine and Surgery.
Be registered with Clinical Officers Council (COC) of Kenya.
With a valid practicing license.
At least three (3) years post qualification working experience.
