RU/AFP/03/12/24
Job Description
Prepare weekly surveillance reports on Malaria and Typhoid to the sub-county disease surveillance department to assist in disease surveillance in the county;
Prepare monthly reports to be submitted to the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Administration, Finance and Planning to plan and monitor the performance of the University laboratory;
Collect, prepare and perform laboratory procedures to assist in the diagnosis, treatment and prevention of diseases as requested by clinicians;
Verify, record and report laboratory results on all performed tests to ensure that the results are correct and accurate;
Maintain cleanliness of laboratory equipment to ensure equipment are in good working condition;
Perform quality control on all lab reagents to ensure accurate results;
Prepare lab reagents to be used in laboratory tests;
Clean and decontaminate surfaces and manage laboratory wastes to prevent spread of infections;
Chart fridge temperatures to ensure reagents are kept at the right temperature for accurate results;
Enter laboratory data in the computer to assist in generation of lab reports; and
Perform any other duty as may be assigned from time to time.
