Job Description
An officer at this level shall:
Provide drug information to patients, clinical officer, nurse and other medical staff;
Timely and accurate posting of dispensed drugs for billing purposes;
Place orders for stock replenishment to the pharmacy store to maintain optimal stock levels;
Participate in regular monitoring of drugs for expiry;
Counsel patients appropriately to ensure adherence to drug therapy;
Participate in stock taking exercise and ensure timely explanation of stock variances;
Enter prescription orders into the computer and making labels appropriately;
Receive drugs and verify against the stock transfer printout;
Perform stock count and stock movement analysis;
Shelving of items appropriately; and
Perform any other duty as may be assigned from time to time.
